<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Isle of Lewis</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Isle of Lewis is the northern part of Lewis and Harris, the largest island of the Outer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrides">Hebrides</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>, with Stornoway as its main town. It holds the Calanais standing stones, and the Lewis chessmen, carved from walrus <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> in the 12th century, were found there in 1831. It was ruled by the Norse kings of Mann and the Isles until 1266.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/isle-of-lewis.jpg" alt="Isle of Lewis" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Julian Paren · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Inner_Stornoway_Harbour_near_Bayhead_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4693267.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
